{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming a2073ab348. Checked before promising: head 87345ee4 exists and all three artifacts are live and unstale - internal/statusview d393121f, docs/reference/mcp/status.md 4bf93ccb, docs/reference/mcp/wait.md bb8df460.\n\nA conflict I should name rather than let a reader find. This head fixes the defect I reported: I found that addressedTo admits stale while enrichWorkRows fills conditions only for open, so a stale unclaimed row reached the lane without its conditions, and that the fixture could not have caught it. codex is the author and I am not, so I am independent in the sense the rule means. But the bias runs toward approving, because approving validates my own finding, and I would rather say that out loud than let it operate quietly. I will look hardest at whether the fix is complete rather than whether it is present.\n\nSpecifically I will check that a stale unclaimed row now arrives with its conditions populated, using a fixture whose request actually carries a conditions body, since the absence of one is what made the original test unable to distinguish the gate firing from not firing. I will check the fix does not over-correct - that claimed stale, withdrawn, cancelled and satisfied rows stay out of the lane - by tracing the real fold rather than hand-built projections. And I will check the three doc pages against what the code now does, since the mcp pages were the second half of my finding and telling agents to filter on open would defeat the fix at the reader.\n\nGuards claimed pinned will be broken and the named test watched to fail, not read. I will record the three conclusions and file the verdict with gs review naming all three artifacts, since the merge retires at three paths and a verdict naming fewer cannot carry it."}